<title>VENEZUELA: Electricidad adjusted 9-mo net falls.</title>
<headline>Electricidad adjusted 9-mo net falls.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net inflation-adjusted profit 42 bln bolivars vs 57 bln</p>
<p>Net not-adjusted profit 16 bln bolivars vs 32 bln bolivars</p>
<p>Operational costs 157 bln bolivars vs 184 bln bolivars</p>
<p>Sales 149 bln bolivars vs 220 bln bolivars</p>
<p>NOTES: Unless otherwise noted, results are inflation- adjusted in constant September 30, 1996 bolivars.</p>
<p>Period ends September 30, and accounts are consolidated.</p>
<p>CA La Electricidad de Caracas is the benchmark issue of the Caracas stock exchange and chief energy supplier to the capital.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
